#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# ellipsoid

#% text
# `ellipsoid([x, y, z], [rx, ry, rz])` is an ellipsoid with semi-axes along the coordinate axes in `graphics3d`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Coordinates are in the units of the graphic; the box around the scene follows the data unless `plot_range` says otherwise.

#% item
# Colours, `opacity` and `edge_form` before it in its list style it; faces are lit.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The default:

#% cell
graphics3d(ellipsoid([0, 0, 0], [2, 1, 1]))
#% output
#= image("ellipsoid.files/ellipsoid-1.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Flattened and stretched:

#% cell
graphics3d([ellipsoid([0, 0, 0], [2, 1, 0.5]), red, ellipsoid([0, 3, 0], [0.5, 0.5, 1.5])])
#% output
#= image("ellipsoid.files/ellipsoid-2.svgz")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# With axes:

#% cell
graphics3d(ellipsoid([0, 0, 0], [1, 2, 3]), axes: true)
#% output
#= image("ellipsoid.files/ellipsoid-3.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `graphics3d`, `sphere`, `plot3d`
